    "task": "text-classification",
    "description": "A compact English ModernBERT cross-encoder trained for natural-language inference and converted by ONNX Community for Transformers.js. It scores contradiction, entailment, and neutrality for premise-hypothesis pairs.",
    "intendedUses": [
      "Compare whether one English statement entails, contradicts, or is neutral toward another.",
      "Prototype lightweight claim consistency and LLM-output evaluation.",
      "Benchmark browser NLI across ONNX precisions and backends."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Designed primarily for English and may degrade on other languages or specialized domains.",
      "Labels are probabilistic model judgments, not logical proofs or factuality guarantees.",
      "Long inputs are truncated at the configured token limit and local attention can miss distant relationships.",
      "Ambiguity, unstated world knowledge, negation, numerical reasoning, and adversarial phrasing can cause errors.",
      "Do not use the classification alone for safety-critical or high-impact decisions."
    ]
  },
